From: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mm/migrate_device: defer folios under writeback

migrate_vma_setup() may collect and lock a folio while writeback is still
in progress. If a driver supplies a destination page, the subsequent
migrate_vma_pages() call reaches BUG_ON(folio_test_writeback(folio)) in
__migrate_device_pages(). A POWER9 NVLink2 ATS access-counter migration
reached this assertion on Linux 6.12.112 and panicked the host.

Migration is best-effort. Skip a source folio still under writeback and
clear its MIGRATE_PFN_MIGRATE flag. migrate_device_finalize() already
handles this failure case: it releases the unused destination, restores
the source page-table entry and unlocks the original folio. The page can
be migrated on a later attempt after writeback completes.

Signed-off-by: eelgaev <3100771+eelgaev@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 mm/migrate_device.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mm/migrate_device.c b/mm/migrate_device.c
--- a/mm/migrate_device.c
+++ b/mm/migrate_device.c
@@ -761,7 +761,16 @@ static void __migrate_device_pages(unsigned long *src_pfns,
 			continue;
 		}
 
-		BUG_ON(folio_test_writeback(folio));
+		/*
+		 * Writeback can outlive the folio lock taken during collection.
+		 * Migration is best-effort: leave this page where it is and let
+		 * migrate_device_finalize() discard the destination and restore
+		 * the source mapping. Do not transfer a folio under writeback.
+		 */
+		if (folio_test_writeback(folio)) {
+			src_pfns[i] &= ~MIGRATE_PFN_MIGRATE;
+			continue;
+		}
 
 		if (migrate && migrate->fault_page == page)
 			extra_cnt = 1;
